## Unitaries intertwining modular objects

A unitary $`V` with $`V\mathcal{M}_1V^{-1} = \mathcal{M}_2` and $`V\Omega_1 = \Omega_2` carries
the Tomita operator, the modular operator, its square root, the modular unitary group and the
modular conjugation of $`(\mathcal{M}_1, \Omega_1)` onto those of $`(\mathcal{M}_2, \Omega_2)`
([thrm:unitary-intertwines-modular-objects](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#thrm:unitary-intertwines-modular-objects)).
For the unbounded objects, "`B = V A V⁻¹`, including domains" is the graph identity
$`\operatorname{graph} B = \Phi_V(\operatorname{graph} A)` with $`\Phi_V(\varphi, \psi) = (V\varphi, V\psi)`;
the general facts about unitary conjugation of unbounded operators, including the transport of
the functional calculus, are in `Physicslib4/Spectral/Unbounded/UnitaryConjugation.lean`.

```lean (name := checkIntertwine)
open Physicslib4 Modular in
#check modular_objects_unitary_intertwine
```

```leanOutput checkIntertwine
Physicslib4.Modular.modular_objects_unitary_intertwine.{u_1} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {M₁ M₂ : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {Ω₁ Ω₂ : H} (hM₁ : IsVonNeumannSet M₁)
  (hM₂ : IsVonNeumannSet M₂) (hΩ₁ : IsCyclicSeparatingVector M₁ Ω₁) (hΩ₂ : IsCyclicSeparatingVector M₂ Ω₂)
  (C₁ C₂ : H ≃ₗᵢ⋆[ℂ] H) (hC₁ : ∀ (x : H), C₁ (C₁ x) = x) (hC₂ : ∀ (x : H), C₂ (C₂ x) = x) (V : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H)
  (hV :
    (fun a => V.toLinearIsometry.toContinuousLinearMap ∘SL a ∘SL V.symm.toLinearIsometry.toContinuousLinearMap) '' M₁ =
      M₂)
  (hVΩ : V Ω₁ = Ω₂) :
  ((∀ (ψ : H),
        ψ ∈ (linearizedTomitaPre M₁ Ω₁ C₁).closure.domain ↔ V ψ ∈ (linearizedTomitaPre M₂ Ω₂ C₂).closure.domain) ∧
      ∀ (ψ : H) (h₁ : ψ ∈ (linearizedTomitaPre M₁ Ω₁ C₁).closure.domain)
        (h₂ : V ψ ∈ (linearizedTomitaPre M₂ Ω₂ C₂).closure.domain),
        tomitaOperator M₂ Ω₂ C₂ ⟨V ψ, h₂⟩ = V (tomitaOperator M₁ Ω₁ C₁ ⟨ψ, h₁⟩)) ∧
    (modularOperator M₂ Ω₂ C₂).graph =
        Submodule.map ((↑V.toLinearEquiv).prodMap ↑V.toLinearEquiv) (modularOperator M₁ Ω₁ C₁).graph ∧
      (modularOperatorSqrt hM₂ hΩ₂ C₂ hC₂).graph =
          Submodule.map ((↑V.toLinearEquiv).prodMap ↑V.toLinearEquiv) (modularOperatorSqrt hM₁ hΩ₁ C₁ hC₁).graph ∧
        (∀ (t : ℝ) (ψ : H),
            V ((modularUnitaryGroup hM₁ hΩ₁ C₁ hC₁ t) (V.symm ψ)) = (modularUnitaryGroup hM₂ hΩ₂ C₂ hC₂ t) ψ) ∧
